Data source: ['Banana', 'Bilberry', 'Blackberry', 'Blackcurrant', 'Blueberry', 'Boysenberry', 'Cranberry']

When user types "b", suggestions filtered: Banana, Bilberry, Blackberry, Blackcurrant, Blueberry, Boysenberry.

Now pressing ArrowDown twice moves selection down two items from the first? Starting selection maybe -1? Usually after opening list, first ArrowDown selects first item (index 0). Two ArrowDowns would select index 1? But the assertion after second ArrowDown expects aria-selected on #autoComplete_result_1 = true. That suggests after two ArrowDowns, the second item (index 1) is selected. Let's verify: Items indices: 0 Banana, 1 Bilberry, 2 Blackberry, 3 Blackcurrant, 4 Blueberry, 5 Boysenberry. After typing "b", list shows those six. ArrowDown once selects index 0 (Banana). ArrowDown again selects index 1 (Bilberry). So assertion expecting #autoComplete_result_1 selected matches Bilberry being selected. Good.

